      "id": 21,
      "options": {
        "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n\nPhase 8B validates fixture-first Codex/OpenAI proxy observability only. This dashboard is not production readiness proof and still includes some copied cache-history panels until real Codex captures verify the right long-term views.\n\n**Codex/OpenAI requests and tokens** come from local fake or proxied Responses traffic observed by coditor-core.\n\n**Context fill** is a bounded histogram of context-window fill percentage; it has provider and normalized model labels only.\n\n**Codex diagnosis causes** show bounded `codex_*` degradation causes. Session ids must not appear in metric labels.\n\n**Cache reuse %** is historical token reuse. For Codex this remains fixture-driven until real cache behavior is captured.\n\n**Model fallbacks** mean the requested model was not the one that actually got used.\n\n**Estimated cost** is a best-effort cost estimate. It is useful for trends, but it may not exactly match billing.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.1.0",
      "title": "Terminology Guide",
      "description": "Short definitions for the dashboard's main terms and KPIs.",
      "type": "text"
    },
